1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,548
Chai Corner is about to
open a second outlet.

2
00:00:03,848 --> 00:00:06,606
But Ravi has never run two stalls at once.

3
00:00:07,156 --> 00:00:09,222
His to-do list is a mess.

4
00:00:09,222 --> 00:00:10,397
Rent a shop.

5
00:00:10,397 --> 00:00:11,504
Hire people.

6
00:00:11,504 --> 00:00:12,554
Buy stoves.

7
00:00:12,854 --> 00:00:15,968
He jumps from job to job,
and finishes nothing.

8
00:00:16,268 --> 00:00:18,896
And opening day is just two weeks away.

9
00:00:19,546 --> 00:00:21,413
Ravi doesn't need more jobs.

10
00:00:21,413 --> 00:00:23,181
He needs the right order.

11
00:00:23,881 --> 00:00:27,241
So Ravi sits down with his
team, over a cup of chai.

12
00:00:27,591 --> 00:00:30,750
Together, they sort every
task into five boxes.

13
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:35,238
Each box is one job that every
manager does, again and again.

14
00:00:35,888 --> 00:00:38,141
These are the functions of management.

15
00:00:38,441 --> 00:00:42,999
The core jobs every manager does,
in every business, of every size.

16
00:00:43,649 --> 00:00:46,491
In 1916, Henri Fayol named five.

17
00:00:46,491 --> 00:00:50,562
Plan, organize, command,
coordinate and control.

18
00:00:50,912 --> 00:00:55,617
In 1937, Luther Gulick stretched it
to seven, and named it by the first

19
00:00:55,617 --> 00:00:56,517
letters.

20
00:00:56,336 --> 00:00:58,952
P, O, S, D, C, O, R, B.

21
00:00:59,302 --> 00:01:01,419
Today, most textbooks use five.

22
00:01:01,419 --> 00:01:05,084
Planning, organizing, staffing,
directing and controlling.

23
00:01:05,734 --> 00:01:08,526
Each function answers one simple question.

24
00:01:08,876 --> 00:01:11,082
Planning asks, what should we do?

25
00:01:11,082 --> 00:01:12,334
Ravi sets a goal.

26
00:01:12,334 --> 00:01:13,923
Two hundred cups a day.

27
00:01:14,273 --> 00:01:16,205
Organizing asks, who does what?

28
00:01:16,205 --> 00:01:19,314
The work is split into
kitchen, counter and cleaning.

29
00:01:19,664 --> 00:01:21,401
Staffing asks, who exactly?

30
00:01:21,401 --> 00:01:24,579
Meena will run the new
outlet, with two new helpers.

31
00:01:24,929 --> 00:01:27,533
Directing asks, how do we guide them?

32
00:01:27,533 --> 00:01:30,088
Asha trains the helpers on her recipe.

33
00:01:30,438 --> 00:01:32,844
And controlling asks, are we on track?

34
00:01:32,844 --> 00:01:35,017
Kabir counts the cups every evening.

35
00:01:35,667 --> 00:01:38,104
One more job holds them all together.

36
00:01:38,104 --> 00:01:39,032
Coordination.

37
00:01:39,032 --> 00:01:42,417
Doing things in the right
order, at the right time.

38
00:01:42,767 --> 00:01:45,954
In Ravi's first plan, the
helpers start on day eight.

39
00:01:45,954 --> 00:01:48,172
But the stoves arrive on day eleven.

40
00:01:48,522 --> 00:01:51,872
That is three days of paid
helpers, with nothing to do.

41
00:01:52,222 --> 00:01:53,876
So Ravi lines them up.

42
00:01:53,876 --> 00:01:56,661
Stoves on day nine, helpers on day ten.

43
00:01:57,011 --> 00:02:00,562
On day fourteen, the new
outlet opens at the bus stand.

44
00:02:00,562 --> 00:02:02,989
Meena runs it, with her two helpers.

45
00:02:03,639 --> 00:02:06,396
Now watch the functions
run, again and again.

46
00:02:06,746 --> 00:02:07,646
Week one.

47
00:02:07,622 --> 00:02:11,639
Kabir's count shows only one
hundred and fifty cups a day.

48
00:02:11,989 --> 00:02:13,707
The goal was two hundred.

49
00:02:13,707 --> 00:02:16,397
So controlling sends
Ravi back to planning.

50
00:02:16,747 --> 00:02:17,661
A new plan.

51
00:02:17,661 --> 00:02:20,347
Open at seven, for the morning bus crowd.

52
00:02:20,697 --> 00:02:24,289
By week four, it sells two
hundred and ten cups a day.

53
00:02:24,289 --> 00:02:25,213
Goal beaten.

54
00:02:25,563 --> 00:02:28,441
That is why the functions
are a cycle, not a list.

55
00:02:29,091 --> 00:02:31,453
So where do you see
these five at work today?

56
00:02:31,803 --> 00:02:32,703
Planning.

57
00:02:32,575 --> 00:02:35,657
A school sets its exam
timetable months ahead.

58
00:02:36,007 --> 00:02:36,925
Organizing.

59
00:02:36,925 --> 00:02:41,635
A hospital splits its work into
wards, like children's and emergency.

60
00:02:41,985 --> 00:02:42,885
Staffing.

61
00:02:42,779 --> 00:02:46,694
An airline hires cabin crew,
then trains them for weeks.

62
00:02:47,044 --> 00:02:47,944
Directing.

63
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:51,437
A cricket captain sets the
field, and keeps the team going.

64
00:02:51,787 --> 00:02:52,687
Controlling.

65
00:02:52,668 --> 00:02:56,393
A delivery app checks every
order against the promised time.

66
00:02:57,043 --> 00:03:00,222
But do real managers
work in this neat order?

67
00:03:00,222 --> 00:03:01,184
Not really.

68
00:03:01,534 --> 00:03:02,577
The good side.

69
00:03:02,577 --> 00:03:05,946
The five functions give a
clear map, for any business.

70
00:03:06,296 --> 00:03:07,441
The hard side.

71
00:03:07,441 --> 00:03:08,950
Real days are messy.

72
00:03:08,950 --> 00:03:11,856
The functions overlap, and happen at once.

73
00:03:12,206 --> 00:03:17,214
In 1973, Henry Mintzberg watched
chief executives at work.

74
00:03:17,564 --> 00:03:20,751
Most of their tasks lasted
less than nine minutes.

75
00:03:21,101 --> 00:03:22,189
So the lesson.

76
00:03:22,189 --> 00:03:24,922
Use the five as a map, not a timetable.

77
00:03:25,572 --> 00:03:26,498
Quick check.

78
00:03:26,498 --> 00:03:30,230
Ravi picks Meena to run the
outlet, and hires two helpers.

79
00:03:30,230 --> 00:03:31,796
Which function is this?

80
00:03:33,696 --> 00:03:34,596
Staffing!

81
00:03:34,474 --> 00:03:37,374
It answers who exactly will fill each job.

82
00:03:37,974 --> 00:03:38,983
So, remember.

83
00:03:39,283 --> 00:03:43,967
The five functions are planning, organizing,
staffing, directing and controlling.

84
00:03:44,317 --> 00:03:45,788
They work as a cycle.

85
00:03:45,788 --> 00:03:47,902
Controlling leads back to planning.

86
00:03:48,252 --> 00:03:51,140
And coordination keeps every part in step.

87
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:55,783
Next time, we'll zoom into the first
function, planning, and how to set

88
00:03:55,783 --> 00:03:56,683
good goals.
